<title>USA: BP says Ohio refinery crude runs remain cut.</title>
<headline>BP says Ohio refinery crude runs remain cut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Petroleum said crude throughput rates remain reduced Tuesday at its Toledo, Ohio, refinery following a Saturday fire.</p>
<p>A BP spokeswoman said there was no change in the status of the investigation into the cause of the fire, or in the reduction of crude unit operations.</p>
<p>A fire struck the 155,000 barrels per day (bpd) refinery on Saturday evening, damaging crude and vacuum distillation units, sources said.</p>
<p>BP refused to specify what parts of the crude facilities were damaged, or the volume rate reduction.</p>
<p>--Patrick Connole, New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1828</p>
</text>
